	(text "Series resistors limit the current of a pin into an input whose supply is absent\n(calculated): RN1 2.2 k: 1.24 mA, 1.39 mA at tolerance. RN4 47 ohm plus R3 1.5 k\nin the DAC select: 1.77 mA, 1.90 mA at tolerance; the inputs of the DAC are rated 2 mA.\nThe slow SPI bus runs at 500 kHz or less."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 143.764 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1aa8abf5-0002-548f-992b-c3a3e134145c")
	)
	(text "Supply: the USB voltage of the module leaves through JP1 as PICO_5V\nto its current limiter (0.76 A) and to the source selector on the Power\nInput sheet, where USB-C has priority. The selected +5V feeds VSYS\nthrough D1. Cut JP1 to keep the carrier off the USB port of the\ncomputer."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.42 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27c005bc-37be-5b51-b22c-ac19c3053915")
	)
	(text "U1 is a Raspberry Pi Pico 2 with headers, plugged into the sockets MP1 and MP2:\nthe only programmable part. RP2350 stepping A3 or A4 is preferred. A Pico 2 W fits\nthe sockets, but the firmware does not support it.\nPIO block 0 (GP16, GP17, GP19 to GP21) clocks the converter and reads its data and the\nside data in the same word. PIO block 1 (GP2 to GP10) is the range sequencer:\ncomparators in, gates and multiplexer address out. J1: TX, RX, GND at 3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8fbeda57-b742-5f64-a41a-744c42efd160")
	)
	(text "Released pins (reset, boot loader, sockets empty): a resistor on the\ncarrier holds every line that the module drives, except the console\noutput. RN2 and RN3 pull the two chip selects (GP13, GP22) up to\n+3V3_A and the other SPI and acquisition lines down: no converter\nis selected, none converts. Against the pad pull-down of the\nRP2350 a select stays at 2.8 V or more (calculated)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 146.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "99b987ce-f21a-5eb6-9a64-33dd7d2f1cc5")
	)
	(text "R1 and R4 keep the two status lines true if a pin is set as an output by mistake:\nVIN_OV then moves by 0.14 V at most, and PWR_GOOD carries 3.3 mA at most (calculated;\nthe comparators that drive it are rated 25 mA). Firmware never sets GP1, GP8 to GP12,\nGP16, GP17 or GP28 as an output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 154.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4134595-3109-5a74-8623-776827249202")
	)
